The `renderFooter()` and `renderToggleAll()` functions are likely culprits—they're probably replacing the entire footer or toggle-all section, which could trigger DOM mutations that Cypress interprets as element detachment. If these functions are rebuilding parts of the DOM, Cypress might lose its reference to elements it was tracking, even if those elements weren't directly modified.

